/// std.result — `Result<T,E>`: success-or-failure as an ordinary
/// generic enum (N23). The type carries NO special machinery — `?`
/// propagation is the operator's desugar (match + early return), and
/// payload authority is plain variant semantics: `Ok(v)` on a `box`
/// moves it, on a `handle` copies identity, on `str` shares the view.
///
/// `expr?` requires `expr : Result<T,E>` and a fn returning
/// `Result<_,E>` — the error type must match exactly; there is no
/// implicit conversion.
pub enum Result<T, E> {
    Ok(T),
    Err(E),
}
